---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Thanksgiving, Christmas, and Holiday Wine Country in Temecula 2026',
  datePublished: '2026-09-25',
  dateModified: '2026-09-25',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bellie Acres Wine' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bellie Acres Wine', url: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/' },
  description: 'Temecula Thanksgiving weekend, Temecula Chilled, ice skating, Old Town lights, and how to taste without fighting parade traffic. Official 2026 links.',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/guides/temecula-holiday-wine-country/',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Thanksgiving and Christmas in Temecula Wine Country 2026"
  description="Temecula Chilled, Peltzer Ice Rink, Holiday Taste of Old Town, Santa’s Electric Light Parade, and tasting-day advice for Thanksgiving through New Year 2026."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="bg-[#faf7f2]">
    <header class="border-b border-stone-200 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
        <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[2px] text-[var(--accent)] font-medium mb-3">Guide · Seasonal · Sep 25, 2026</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif tracking-tight text-stone-900 leading-[1.1]">
          Thanksgiving through New Year in Temecula
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg sm:text-xl text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
          There is no single “Temecula Thanksgiving festival” that replaces a family table. What you get instead is
          Shop Small weekend, then a month of lights, ice, and tasting rooms under the
          <a class="underline" href="https://www.visittemeculavalley.com/temecula-chilled/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Temecula Chilled</a>
          umbrella (day after Thanksgiving through December 31). Plan the table first, the lights second, and the
          tasting third — or you will sit in Old Town traffic with a cold flight waiting.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 space-y-6 text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-2">Thanksgiving week</h2>
      <p>
        Thanksgiving Day 2026 is Thursday, November 26. Many tasting rooms run reduced hours or close so staff can be
        with family. Do not assume a walk-in flight exists that afternoon. Call the estate or use the
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/wineries">wineries list</a> as a starting point, then confirm
        the holiday hours on the winery’s own site.
      </p>
      <p>
        Friday–Saturday, November 27–28, Old Town lists
        <strong>Shop Small Weekend</strong> (Black Friday and Small Business Saturday) and
        <strong>Santa’s Arrival at Pennypickle’s Workshop</strong> Friday evening, with weekend Santa hours after that.
        Official: <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://oldtowntemecula.org/events-tickets/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Old Town Temecula events</a>.
        If relatives want a stroll, that is the civic program. If they want wine, book Friday or Sunday on a corridor
        away from Front Street.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-2">Temecula Chilled and ice</h2>
      <p>
        Visit Temecula Valley frames winter as
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://www.visittemeculavalley.com/temecula-chilled/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Temecula Chilled</a>:
        Wine Country, Old Town, and Pechanga each running their own holiday programming after Thanksgiving. Use that
        hub for the seasonal overlay; use our
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/events">events list</a> for the dated items we have checked.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://www.peltzerfarms.com/peltzer-ice-rink" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Peltzer Ice Rink</a>
        is listed as closed until November 2026, with Visit Temecula Valley showing sessions from about
        <strong>November 19, 2026 into January 2027</strong>. Sessions are reserved, rain or shine, 21+ bar on site.
        That is a family block, not a substitute for a tasting reservation. If you skate and taste the same day, skate
        first, eat, then one estate — not the reverse.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-2">December lights, taste, and parade</h2>
      <p>
        Old Town’s own 2026 calendar (stronger than a third-party roundup) currently lists:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Dec 1–26</strong> — A Very Temecula Christmas window walk (self-guided storefronts).</li>
        <li><strong>Dec 3, 5:00–8:30 p.m.</strong> — Holiday Taste of Old Town (ticketed stroll). Tickets typically release about a month out on the same <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://oldtowntemecula.org/events-tickets/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Old Town events page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Dec 4, 7:00 p.m.</strong> — Santa’s Electric Light Parade on Front Street (OTTA listing; some city calendars still say Dec 5 — confirm the week of).</li>
        <li><strong>Dec 10–12</strong> — A Very Temecula Christmas weekend, including a holiday boutique crawl and Cars, Cocoa &amp; Carolers.</li>
        <li><strong>Dec 12</strong> — Santa under the Civic Center tree.</li>
        <li><strong>Dec 31, 6:00–10:00 p.m.</strong> — New Year’s Eve Grape Drop at the Civic Center Quad.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Parade night is the worst night to “just swing by a tasting room in Old Town.” Front Street is the show. Book
        wine country itself — Rancho California or De Portola — and come into Old Town after the last float, or skip
        wine that evening.
      </p>
      <p>
        Old Town Temecula Community Theater also lists
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="https://www.visittemeculavalley.com/event/a-christmas-carol-the-musical/12303/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A Christmas Carol, The Musical (Dec 5–13, 2026)</a>.
        That is a seated night. Pair it with lunch tasting, not a three-stop afternoon.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-stone-900 pt-2">How this fits a tasting plan</h2>
      <p>
        Holiday weeks are reservation weeks. Estates host private dinners, clubs, and early closures. Use the
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/map">wine map</a> to cluster two nearby rooms, then protect
        time for lights. Sparkling and lighter reds suit heavy meals; our
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-sparkling-wine-guide">sparkling guide</a>
        and
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-wine-and-food-pairing-day">food-and-wine day</a>
        are the pairing pages, not this calendar.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Halloween and pumpkin farms, use
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-halloween-fall-family">Halloween and fall family days</a>.
        For stomps earlier in fall, stay on the
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/temecula-fall-wine-events-guide">grape stomp guide</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">
        Independent overview. We do not sell tickets. Confirm every date with the organizer.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
